    "content": "Eleven (11) is the natural number following 10 and preceding 12. It is the first two-digit prime number, a repdigit (11), and a prime number. In English, it originates from Old English endleofan, meaning \"one left\" over after ten. It is often associated with the \"eleventh hour\" (urgency) and 11-player sports teams. Key Aspects of 11: Mathematics: 11 is a prime number, the base of the undecimal system, and is represented as 10+1. Time & Measurement: Represents the 11th hour (11:00) and November, the 11th month. Symbolism: Often linked to themes of intuition, spiritual insight, and enlightenment in numerology. Technology & Culture: Frequently used in naming (e.g., Windows 11, iPhone 11) and refers to a \"master number\" or a \"perfect marriage\" metaphor where 1+1=11. Windows 11 iPhone 11 Common Phrases: \"Up to eleven\": Coined by This Is Spinal Tap to signify going beyond normal limits. \"Eleventh hour\": Refers to the last possible moment.",
